Komport-Qt6
===========

A serial port communicator and VT100/VT102 terminal emulator for Linux,
built on Qt6 and QSerialPort.

This is a maintained continuation of "Komport" by Mike Sharkey (2003), a
KDE 2/3 application whose upstream project is no longer maintained. All
KDE Frameworks and Qt3 dependencies have been removed; the terminal
emulation, character-grid rendering and general application structure are
carried forward. See CLAUDE.md for the full picture of what changed and
why, and TODO.md for the detailed migration/feature log.

Notable features beyond the original:
  - Serial backend on QSerialPort/QSerialPortInfo (device autodetection,
    proper data bits/stop bits/parity/flow control)
  - Toggleable hex monitor (RX/TX, split-screen, classic [offset][hex][ascii])
  - Fuller VT100/VT102 emulation (DECCKM, DECTCEM, insert/delete line/char,
    device status reports, extended SGR colors)
  - Programmable quick-command macro buttons
  - One-click, timestamped session logging
  - Configurable line ending (CR/LF/CR+LF) for the Return key and macros

